course: dictionary
lesson: 5752
title: Many meanings of low
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word low can change its meaning from one sentence to the next. Context tells you which meaning to use. «A seat belt's lap part goes low across the hips» means near the bottom, not sad or quiet, because the words around it are about where the belt sits on the body.
explain: Check the clues around the word. In «Keep your voice low in the library», low means quiet, because a library is a place for quiet. In «She is feeling low today», low means sad or tired, because the word feeling tells you it is about a mood.
explain: Low can also be a noun. «The rain brought a new low» means the lowest point, a level below all the others. Put your chosen meaning back into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Low can be an adjective, an adverb or a noun, so it can work in different kinds of sentences.
fact: «Low» means not high, close to the ground or the bottom, as in «a low wall».
fact: «Low» means small in number, amount or level, as in «a low price» or «low temperature» (cold).
fact: «Low» can mean deep or quiet for a sound, and it can mean sad or tired when you are «feeling low».
exercise: «A loaded ship sits lower in the water.» What does lower mean here? | *Nearer the bottom, sitting deeper | Lighter in colour | Higher above the waves | Faster across the sea
exercise: «Keep your voice low in the library.» What does low mean here? | Happy | Tall | Very loud | *Quiet
exercise: «Walking sharks can survive when a rock pool gets warm and stale at low tide.» What does low tide mean? | A big storm at sea | When the sea is at its highest level | A very deep rock pool | *When the sea is at its lowest level
test: «Her phone has a low battery.» What does low mean here? | *Small amount left | Very loud | Very high | Bright and shiny
test: Mia says «I feel low today». What does low mean? | Very quick | Very tall | Standing on the ground | *Sad or tired
exam: «The rain brought a new low.» What does a new low mean? | A quiet, gentle sound | *The lowest point or number so far | A new lower case letter | A new hill to climb
